# Vault & Bind-Mount Data Protection

## Hard ban (production GREEN: 68.183.168.75)
NEVER execute against /opt/clinical-sovereignty-lab/data/ or any bind-mounted volume:
- docker compose ... --force-recreate (specifically forbidden)
- docker compose down -v (anonymous volume removal)
- rm -rf data/, rm -rf Vaults/
- rsync --delete with data/ as target
- find data/ -delete
- git clean -fd (will wipe untracked data/ even with .gitignore)

## Required wrapper
All production docker compose actions go through:
  /opt/clinical-sovereignty-lab/scripts/safe_deploy.sh <service>

The wrapper:
1. Tar-snapshots data/bridge/Vaults and data/backend/Vaults before deploy
2. Counts metrics.json files pre-deploy
3. Runs docker compose up -d <service> (no --force-recreate, no --build flags unless caller explicitly passes)
4. Counts metrics.json files post-deploy
5. Exit code 2 + ALERT if count drops more than 10%

## Vault file ownership after writes

**Rule:** Any vault file write from **host** or **container** (one-off/root) must end with **`chown 1000:1000`** + **`chmod 644`** on the files touched.

Typical commands after the write:

```bash
chown 1000:1000 <path>
chmod 644 <path>
```

(Apply to the concrete file or directory tree you just wrote, as appropriate.) The bridge container runs as **UID/GID 1000** (`nate`). Default root-owned or mode `600` files cause `[Errno 13] Permission denied` for `MetricsEngine` / `parietal` on `/app/data/Vaults/...`.

**Reference:** 2026-05-12 — host-side metrics.json fixes created `root:root` `600`; replay via `docker exec nate_bridge` failed until ownership/mode were corrected.

## Why
2026-05-12 02:56:22 UTC incident: --force-recreate during deploy wiped /data/bridge/Vaults/Clients/ (28 days of accumulated metrics for 26 clients, ~826 files). Root cause: bind mount detached during 2-second container kill-restart gap; new bridge container lazy-initialized empty files via initialize_metrics() default stub.
